==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|amonge}} {{qualifier|archaic}}
* {{l|en|amoung}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|id=mingling|inh|enm>among>mingling|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|among}}, {{m|enm|amang}}, {{m|enm|amonge}}, {{m|enm|amange}}, from {{inh|en|ang|amang}}, {{m|ang|onġemang}}, equivalent to {{prefix|en|a|mong|t2=crowd; group; throng}}. Cognate with {{cog|stq|monk}}, {{m|stq|monken|t=among}}, {{cog|fy|mank|t=among}}, {{cog|nl|mank}}, {{m|nl|maank|t=among}}, {{cog|nds-de|mank}}, {{m|nds-de|manken|t=among}}, dialectal {{cog|de|mang|t=among}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əˈmʌŋ/|/əˈmɒŋ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-among.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyphenation|en|a|mong}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌŋ|s=2}}

===Preposition===
{{en-prep}}

# Denotes a [[mingling]] or [[intermixing]] with distinct or separable objects. (See Usage Note at [[amidst]].)
#: {{ux|en|How can you speak with authority about their customs when you have never lived '''among''' them?}}
# Denotes a [[belong]]ing of a person or a thing to a group.
#: {{ux|en|He is '''among''' the few who completely understand the subject.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-08-10|volume=408|issue=8848|magazine=w:The Economist
|title=[http://www.economist.com/news/leaders/21583277-worlds-biggest-polluter-going-green-it-needs-speed-up-transition-can-china Can China clean up fast enough?]
|passage=All this has led to an explosion of protest across China, including '''among''' a middle class that has discovered nimbyism.}}
# Denotes a [[share|sharing]] of a [[common]] feature in a group.
#: {{ux|en|Lactose intolerance is common '''among''' people of Asian heritage.}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Luke|1|1|passage=Forasmuch as many have taken in hand to set forth in order a declaration of those things which are most surely believed '''among''' us […]}}

====Usage notes====
* For the comparison of ''among'' with ''between'', see the usage notes in ''[[between]]''.
* Many Americans view "amongst" as an archaic/Commonwealth variant, and use "among" exclusively.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|amongst}} (variant of among, slightly [[Appendix:Glossary#dated|dated]])
* {{l|en|amidst}}
* {{l|en|amid}}

